# 050 · A two-command start, and a generated settings reference

**Status:** `PROPOSED` · **Version:** [v0.6.0](../roadmap.md#v060)

## What

`thermite init`, `up`, `down`, `status` and `demo` start and run Thermite from the published images. The docs site's settings reference is generated from the code. The docs site itself is goal [060](_completed/060-docs-site.goal).

## Why

Two commands are easier than a compose file. A generated settings reference cannot drift from the code.

## Done when

- [ ] `thermite init && thermite up` gives a running control and rig.
- [ ] The settings reference is generated from the code, and CI fails when it is out of date.

## Decisions

None yet.

## Open questions

None.

## Progress

- 2026-10-19: Goal written from the roadmap.
- 2026-10-19: The docs site moved to goal [060](_completed/060-docs-site.goal) in v0.1.0. This goal keeps the two-command start and the generated settings reference.

